{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T23:45:17.865151Z","id":"2911887052c33d4a9958be886a4fc28e912698a480959e8784c4d2b305a0e638","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1121},"end":{"line":1165},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"suggested_fix":"Settle the meaning in spec §8.3; count withheld fields instead if the shell or tools need it.","summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"0e680b4f21f675c8aaea03389d24a2c34293a97dd279aa77e946917bcf25a5b5","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T23:46:47.443414Z","id":"e674ac51496c594134df3876d02e982993bd1094fbf393a82c2f429bf7bed2e9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:603fc8f","summary":"Fixed: the docs routes are open to a person's agent and each write route refuses its x-clax-via: page. api_visibility::a_persons_agent_never_writes_documents_as_a_page sends PUT, PATCH, DELETE …/docs/{*path}, docs:batch, docs:str_replace and docs:acquire as Sam's agent with the marker, from its session and without one: each answers 400 invalid_via_page, and no document, lease or author changes (cargo test -p clax-server --test integration -- api_visibility:: : 30 passed, 0 failed). Mutation: making CallerParts ignore the marker for a grant fails that test.","supersedes":"28e2f708c283ec49b60a239dc76fbe14af843559bec3d366a5c29114f13f111f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/push.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.793803Z","id":"8a284a422bdbeef141d25470cf1dc899c1a76e20313674371be797242a932eb4","body":{"detail":"dispatch runs only for Touched targets (a send, a retarget, a release). An approval or revocation bumps the visibility generation, which wakes long-polls (routes/feedback.rs wait_for_change) but runs no dispatch, so an idle Codex session with armed watches gets the newly visible rows only from its next tool call, hook or wait. No route makes approvals yet (the approvals routes are to come); when one lands it should dispatch to the approver's live Codex sessions.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":204},"end":{"line":204},"content_hash":"af90eb658a65c860feb6c5f30f8abdfd60d2becfda0a4562bb30ec85db0952e0"},"summary":"An approval does not push to a Codex session: rows it lets through wait for the session's next in-band take","tags":["people","spec:9.3","depends:approval-routes","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.794590Z","id":"1e09aa1e3fcacb3e14216e53982ce149b9e74339abed9223145ba1a1e294b980","body":{"detail":"api_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":477},"end":{"line":477},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","tags":["people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:55.166289Z","id":"cbc878e00c3498a04d1495adc8cd503452b547123c3b92187b0ad3cc9dad595d","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":920},"end":{"line":920},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"cc1947157a229c2dad683481e31f66b05a5043da159f0e63a3ee413b1f10f418","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
